q('What LDL-C response generally defines high-intensity statin therapy?', 'An expected reduction of at least 50%',[
 ('An expected reduction below 10%','That is not high intensity.'),('A rise in HDL alone without LDL change','Intensity is defined by expected LDL reduction.'),('An identical fixed final LDL in every person','Baseline and individual response vary.')],
 'Intensity describes expected effect, not guaranteed individual response', '**Examples include appropriate high doses of atorvastatin or rosuvastatin.**',['Tolerability and interactions affect the achievable regimen.','The absolute goal and percentage reduction both inform follow-up.'], '**Check response after initiation or dose change.**',['Review adherence and secondary causes if the effect is unexpectedly small.','Use additional agents when risk-based goals remain unmet.'],[['High intensity','At least 50% expected reduction'],['Moderate intensity','Usually 30–49%'],['Follow-up','Measured response and tolerance']],[LI])
